        "created_at": "2017-08-24T12:55:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TakeWalker wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Yeah, I was wondering about that. His base incap shows him targeting Parse and Setback, though, so I would imagine his deck represents how he operated before Oblivaeon.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSome incaps take place before the deck happens. One of Ex-Patriette's incaps shows her losing her eye.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>None of her incaps shows that. &nbsp; She lost her eye before she left the Citizens originally. &nbsp; The incap I think you're referencing is her defeat by the Citizens when she went after them herself when they invaded Megaopolis and is right before Scholar picks her up in Don't Dismiss Anything</p>",
